.TH SNIFFNET 1 "September 2026" "Sniffnet 1.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sniffnet \- comfortably monitor network traffic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sniffnet
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sniffnet provides a graphical overview of network traffic, including bandwidth usage, connections, protocols, remote hosts and programs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-adapter " [NAME]"
Start capturing packets from the supplied network adapter. If NAME is omitted, use the configured adapter.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config-path
Print the path to the configuration file and exit.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-restore-default
Restore default settings and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sniffnet
Open the graphical interface.
.TP
.B sniffnet \-\-adapter eth0
Start capturing on eth0.
.SH FILES
Run
.B sniffnet \-\-config-path
to find the current user's configuration file.
.SH NOTES
The Debian package configures network capabilities on the executable so ordinary users can capture traffic.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://sniffnet.app
Sniffnet website
.UE
